  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 135 PM CST Mon Nov 2 2026\n\nPresent model agreement does see active weather return to the\nPanhandles Wednesday with current runs seeing yet another trough\nbrush the Northern Panhandles late that night into Thursday\nmorning. Unfortunately, the northerly position of this trough has\nseen many of the models keeping activity contained to the Oklahoma\nPanhandles and the far Northeastern Texas Panhandles with chances\nonly around 10 to 30 percent. Moving into the later hours of\nThursday, most models do see another ridge building in across the\nSouthwestern United States, which will lead to northwesterly\nupper-level flow across the Panhandles. Under this flow the\nPanhandles has a tendency to keep to a more active pattern thanks\nto it being easier to force short-wave into the area. However,\npresent agreement between the ensembles has not really seen that\npotential manifest, with current trends now dropping our chance of\nprecipitation below 10 percent through the weekend. Regardless,\ntemperature will stay cool under this flow with afternoon highs\nholding in the low to mid 60s.",
